  texts:
  - Name: HowIMetYourMaid
    Text: I saw her and she was there
    IsInJournal: 0
  - Name: TheArgonianMaid
    Text: Example text, not for sale
    IsInJournal: 0
  - Name: Note(80YearsAgo)
    Text: "I have never seen anything quite like this place. Even the brightest fire
      could not light this place more than a couple meters. It is hard just writing
      this note. \r\nAll my companions are gone. They started muttering to themselves
      before running off into the dark. I have started to hear voices calling out
      to me. I fear I might suffer the same fate as the rest of them. If i don\u2019t
      come back then please. To whoever poor fool is reading this. Turn back. Whatever
      it is that's hiding in here is not worth it.  \r\n\r\n-Henrik Alfson, 1198\r\n"
    IsInJournal: 1
  - Name: Note(Edwards)
    Text: "Edwards journal. \r\nEntry 15\r\nThe numerous tales of the so-called \u201CAgathol\u201D
      have led me to the city of G\xFCnhildr where it was said to lie. It turns out
      the rumors were true. This place is crawling with seasoned and amateur explorers
      alike, all roaring to get to the bottom of the dungeon and loot whatever treasures
      are hidden within. Although I have heard some more concerning tales as well.
      Apparently people rarely return. and the few that do often aren't too happy
      to talk about it. \r\nI can't quite wrap my head around why so many people
      are risking their lives to explore that place. Although, I myself have gotten
      a strange inclination to do the same.\r\n\r\n"
    IsInJournal: 1
  - Name: Note(JessJournal)
    Text: "Jess\u2019s journal\r\n\r\nEver since I got here to Gunhildr all I hear
      is Agathol this and Agathol that. Is there truly nothing else in this CITY,
      mind you, than this blasted dungeon? That\u2019s what most of the locals seem
      to convey at least. I don\u2019t get it. It doesn\u2019t seem that out of the
      ordinary from what I can gather.\r\n\r\nTURNPAGE\r\n\r\nI get it now, I now
      see why so many venture down. Everything is down there. Everything I could
      ever want, everything I\u2019ll ever need. I\u2019ll be there soon, Agathol.\r\n\r\n"
    IsInJournal: 1
  - Name: Note(RuinFun)
    Text: "October 19, 1273. We finally found something worth bringing back. Well
      \u201Cworth\u201D is a strong word. All it is a purple gemstone. probably an
      amethyst of some kind. probably barely worth 50 crowns. I told the others such
      but they all snapped at me. Going on about me \u201Cruining their fun\u201D?
      \r\nI don't get it. These shitheads have gotten weird.  \r\n\r\nTURNPAGE\r\n\r\nWhY
      DO yOu RuIN OuR fUNn??\r\n"
    IsInJournal: 1
  - Name: Note(SacredGods)
    Text: "Oh sacred gods above the stars, If you can hear me, please answer my prayers
      true. This place is profane beyond anything else in this mortal realm. And
      so I beg thee cast this hell out of our world so it may never defile any other
      poor soul untouched by your grace.\r\n\r\nPlease I beg you\u2026 Why? Why is
      it the voice of the damned I hear, and not that of yours?\r\n\r\nTURNPAGE\r\n\r\nI
      can see it now, clear as the brightest star. The answers, The answers to it
      all. They are found here. We should not run from it. We should not fear it.
      We should not reject it. \r\nWE SHOULD EMBRACE IT. WE SHOULD BECOME IT. FOR
      AGATHOL IS ALL. AGATHOL IS EVERYTHING. WHY DIDN\u2019T I REALIZE?\r\nWE ARE
      AGATHOL AND AGATHOL WILL GRANT US TRUTH.\r\n\r\n"
    IsInJournal: 1
  - Name: Note(ScorchedSword)
    Text: "William Regin\u2019s notebook\r\n\r\n\u201CChapter 4, The Scorched Sword.\u201D\r\nThe
      Great dragon Xayoc was once said to have forged a blade of pure flame that
      he dubbed \u201CThe Scorched Sword\u201D which he later threw away into the
      depths of an unknown crypt when he was driven back in the War of the Mountain.
      \r\nI believe that there is no better option than for him to have hidden it
      in Agathol. Or it is at least the best option. No other similar \u201Ccrypts\u201D
      have ever been discovered near where said conflict was fought and if all of
      my family's stories are to be believed then that place seems like a perfect
      spot to hide such a relic.\r\nHowever, most of them seem to dismiss my theory. 
      \u201CThere may  be treasure down there but not that of fairy tales\u201D they
      say. Even so, you can't prove a negative. I will descend into Agathol like
      my forefathers before me and prove them all wrong. \r\n\r\n\r\n"
    IsInJournal: 1
  - Name: Note(Syn'sMother)
    Text: "To Syn\r\n\r\nForgive me Syn. Your mother has been very foolish.\r\nI
      know you will probably never see this but on the off chance you do I need you
      to know I\u2019m very proud of you. Even though you hide your feelings behind
      your harsh words, I can tell that you really do care about the people around
      you. And I think they know too. \r\nYet I still went down here thinking I\u2019d
      find something. And I can\u2019t even remember what it was.\r\nSyn.. I\u2019m
      sorry. I\u2019m sorry that I\u2019ll never get to see you again. I\u2019m sorry
      that I couldn\u2019t be a better mother. Do tell your father that I love him
      okay? And say hi to Alva from me. And of course.\r\nI love you Syn. I hope
      you live a long and happy life.\r\n"
    IsInJournal: 1
  - Name: Note(WanderingCorpse)
    Text: "\u201DLog entry 18\u201D\r\n\r\nNone of the anecdotes could have prepared
      me for this place. I had heard from a previous adventurer that this place was
      wicked but that proved to be an understatement. I\u2019ve seen countless people
      down here. But they all act like wandering corpses. They mutter nonsense and
      go on and on about Agathol. Some even bolted for me when they noticed my presence
      but I somehow managed to escape.\r\nI believe it\u2019s safe to assume that
      \u201DAgathol\u201D has possessed them somehow. And I have a hypothesis as
      to what might be causing it. The dark.\r\nWhenever my torch flickers I can
      hear faint voices calling out to me. Calling out \u201DAgathol\u201D.\r\nI
      pray I can get out of here before my only light goes out.\r\n"
    IsInJournal: 1
  - Name: Note(Children)
    Text: "They are children, the children are everywhere. No matter where I look,
      where I touch they are there. They may be on my very body without my knowledge.
      I\u2019m afraid. I can\u2019t find the way out. My trail was eaten by the hidden
      children. The hidden children will be my death.\r\n\r\nNEXTPAGE\r\n\r\n<color=#800000ff><b>THEY
      ARE IN MY SKIN, IN MY SKIN, IN MY SKIN. I NEED THEM OUT OUT OUT OUT OUT OUT.
      GET GET GET GET GET THEM ou-.</b></color>\r\n"
    IsInJournal: 0
